beat_this_final0.w8.onnx — learned beat + downbeat tracker, converted for in-browser inference.
Log-mel spectrogram in ([1, frames ≤ 1500, 128]: 22.05 kHz, 50 frames/s, 128 Slaney mels 30 Hz–11 kHz,
log1p(1000·x)); beat and downbeat logits out ([1, frames]). The spectrogram is computed outside the graph
(engine.tsx beatThisLogMel, held to beat_this's own LogMelSpect by tests/fixtures/beatthis-features.json).

Model:          beat_this "final0" — Francesco Foscarin, Jan Schlüter, Gerhard Widmer, "Beat this! Accurate
                beat tracking without DBN postprocessing" (ISMIR 2024, arXiv:2407.21658);
                code https://github.com/CPJKU/beat_this (commit b95c8ab0c58c2d9fcfd40508ae8dffbc05ac4f5c).
Weights:        final0.ckpt, 81,058,141 bytes, SHA-256
                8c328b45f59d8dd3dff219253ff6a8d6482be57d0133a29140e2febbf8eb8331. The official host
                (cloud.cp.jku.at) was not reachable from the build environment; the file was taken from two
                independent Hugging Face re-uploads (oulianov/beat_this, teamup-tech/Beat-This-weights),
                which are byte-identical. License: MIT (code and published weights, per the README).
Conversion:     scripts/beatthis_export.py — fp32 ONNX, opset 17, dynamic time axis (matches PyTorch to 2.2e-6
                at 1500 / 1129 / 64 frames), then weight-only int8 (per-channel scale + DequantizeLinear;
                activations stay fp32). On 12 GuitarSet recordings the int8 file puts 548 of 557 beats and
                265 of 268 downbeats within one frame of PyTorch.

